STANDARDS FOR IMPOSING ADMINISTRATIVE FINES (Article 20)
1. General Standards
(a) Aggravated standards based on violation frequency apply if a fine for the same violation was imposed in the preceding year. Calculate the period from the date of that fine disposition to the date the same violation is detected after it.
(b) When aggravating under item (a), apply the stage immediately following the previous disposition's stage (the highest stage if two or more fine dispositions occurred in that period).
(c) In any of the following cases, the authority may reduce the fine under section 2 by up to one-half, except for a violator with overdue administrative fines:
1) The violation is attributable to negligence such as minor carelessness or error;
2) Its particulars and gravity are minor and social harm is considered small;
3) The violator is recognized as having tried to correct or eliminate the unlawful condition;
4) Reduction is otherwise considered necessary in view of gravity, motivation, consequences, and other circumstances.
